      <description>&lt;p&gt;This blog is mainly a note taking of &lt;a href=&#34;https://mit-mi.github.io/mmai-course/spring2026/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noreferrer&#34;&gt;MIT MMAI&lt;/a&gt; in spring 2026. After watching the video on YouTube, fairly to say, this course lacks technical details comparing to &lt;a href=&#34;https://morethan987.github.io/en/blog/llm-training-playbook/&#34; &gt;CS336&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&#34;https://morethan987.github.io/en/blog/flow-matching-and-diffusion/&#34; &gt;MIT 6.S184&lt;/a&gt;. Maybe one main reason for this is some lecture videos are not public. Some courses offer slide but not video (see in &lt;a href=&#34;https://mit-mi.github.io/mmai-course/spring2026/schedule/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noreferrer&#34;&gt;schedule&lt;/a&gt;). And there is no offical homework repository but some students from MIT uploaded the homework to GitHub. Here is one &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/hangzhao1006/Multi-Modal-AI&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noreferrer&#34;&gt;repo&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
